  A modular castle and town wall kit sheet for an isometric pixel art game, on a plain flat light grey background, pieces separated with space between them, all at the same scale, in exactly the style of the reference image (same pixel size, outline, palette and shading). 16-bit SNES pixel art, isometric 2:1 projection, warm earthy palette (browns, tans, terracotta, forest green, stone grey, gold, deep red, sky blue), single dark outline, medium shading, light from the top left, medieval central European, 14th century. Crisp pixels, no blur, no text, no UI. Pieces: straight crenellated curtain wall segment in both isometric directions, inner and outer wall corner, square wall tower, round wall tower with conical slate roof, gatehouse with portcullis and wooden gate, wall stairs, a ruined wall segment, a wooden hoarding segment; and on the right a small assembled castle made from the same pieces. Two 1.7 m tall soldiers stand at the gate for scale; the wall is about five times their height.

